        "cnm_224"
      ],
      "explanation": "Because the base \\(2\\) is greater than \\(1\\), \\(2^t\\) is strictly increasing. Thus \\(2^t=1=2^0\\) holds exactly when \\(t=0\\). The given equation is therefore equivalent to\n\\[\n2x^2-7x+5=0.\n\\]\nFactoring gives\n\\[\n(2x-5)(x-1)=0,\n\\]\nso \\(x=5/2\\) or \\(x=1\\). Both values make the original exponent zero, and the factorization shows there are no others. Hence there are \\(\\boxed{2}\\) real values, choice C.",
